  "independent_scope": "Whole native selected-source content on both mattes, all9 selected poses plus adopted neutral at inherited maximum body reference 140.000000px across5both-matte pages, and all7 decoded discrete recipe rows actually viewed. Historical unselected sheet cells are not accepted by viewing their whole source. Physical UI zoom/density and real-time/interpolated/MP4 output not measured.",
  "observations": "Actually inspected whole1254 core sheet on both mattes and the fixed right-facing single on both mattes, all9 selected poses beside adopted neutral across5full-fit inherited140px body-reference pages, and all7 decoded discrete recipes. Navy dorsal band, blue-gray middle, cream belly, solid brown dot eye, two principal dorsal fins, yellow rear finlets and one forked crescent tail remain recognizable and clean. Closed blink keeps the usual body length, dorsal/tail layout and center closely; expression changes alone are intentional. Greet lifts the connected near pectoral fin; left presentation uses the connected near fin while retaining left gaze. Fresh present_right genuinely faces right and extends its near fin right, with intact fin roots and tail. The reversed view has a slightly different width/projection but no obvious body-scale regression. Think dips the head, aha raises it and cheer lifts the connected fin/body expression. Species phases flex the same single tail up/down without duplicated appendages. All selected eyes, gills, fin roots and finlet silhouettes remain clear at140px. Watercolor/paper grain stays bounded inside color shapes; no broad color field, dirty patches, transparency cuts or unintended extra anatomy was seen. The old left-facing rejected present_right cell was visible only as history in the whole core sheet and was not accepted. Dynamic independent comparison panels keep the complete tail in view; no original PNG cut was seen.",
